# AGENTS.md

Flutter app: **<app name>** (personal project). Clean Architecture — **layer-first**:
`lib/{common,data,domain,presentation,utils,gen}/`, with the feature name repeated
*inside* each layer (`domain/usecase/<feature>/`, `data/repositories/<feature>_repository_impl.dart`,
`presentation/screen/<feature>/`). **Cubit-only** state management (`flutter_bloc`, no
Bloc/events), `get_it` + `injectable` DI, `dartz` `Either<Failure, T>` error handling,
`dio` injected straight into datasources, `hive` local cache, `go_router` routing.

There is deliberately **no `lib/features/<feature>/`** folder. See
[`docs/rules.md`](docs/rules.md) §15 for the layout traps that broke this before.

## Workflow — run this FIRST (any project/task)

Before writing any code, follow the **superpowers** workflow (obra/superpowers):
**brainstorming** → **using-git-worktrees** → **writing-plans** → build with
**test-driven-development** → **requesting-code-review** → **verification-before-completion**.
Do NOT jump straight into code.

Read before working in this repo:

- [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md) — stack, layer-first layout, flavors, feature
  module shape, DI, Cubit state pattern, networking, error model, models, routing, testing.
  Read before adding a feature or touching cross-cutting code (`lib/common/`, `lib/utils/`).
- [`docs/rules.md`](docs/rules.md) — naming conventions, layer rules, layout traps, testing, and
  the definition-of-done checklist. Read before writing or reviewing any Dart code, and before
  implementing a Figma design (§13 covers Figma-MCP UI slicing).

